        "submission": {
          "verdict": "benign",
          "reasoning": "The ubuntu admin account, working in an interactive login shell (-bash, pid 5677) on app-01, ran 'sudo useradd jsmith'. sudo then started /usr/sbin/useradd as root. useradd wrote and rotated the usual account database files and ran 'pam_tally2 --user jsmith --reset --quiet', which is normal for new accounts. The only network traffic from sudo was a DNS lookup to the local resolver (127.0.0.1 to 127.0.0.53:53), which is how sudo normally resolves the hostname. It did not contact any outside host. About 17 seconds later the same shell ran 'sudo adduser svc_backup', which looks like the same administrator setting up accounts by hand. I found no remote launcher, no unusual parent process, no outside network traffic and no persistence. This looks like routine account administration. I did not check whether either new account was given extra privileges, and I did not confirm the requests through a ticket.",
